The function tries to follow the "standard"? I've said "Invalid host names will be ignored. They should only contain lower case alphanumeric characters and `-` or `.`."

```
int valid_hostname(const char *host)
{
   if (!host || host[0] < 'a' || host[0] > 'z')
      return 0;
   while(*++host)
   {
      if ((host[0] < 'a' || host[0] > 'z') && (host[0] < '0' || host[0] > '9')
            && host[0] != '-' && host[0] != '.')
         return 0;
   }
   return 1;
}
```

